+# D3DMetal port from CrossOver 26
+
+Target: Nectarine's `d3dmetal` branch, starting at `8d038d8c9bc` (Proton
+bleeding-edge Wine 11 plus the existing macOS commits). Reference: the supplied
+read-only, flattened `../cxwine-ref` source directories. No Apple binaries or
+source from other CrossOver directories are included.
+
+The runtime opt-in is the exact, case-sensitive value
+`CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=d3dmetal`. The Unix bridge additionally uses
+`CX_APPLEGPTK_LIBD3DSHARED_PATH`. Set these before starting Wine. All new host
+specific behavior is restricted to Apple/x86_64. PE code cannot use `__APPLE__`
+(the PE compiler targets Windows); its small compatibility hooks use x86_64 and
+an explicit environment check instead. Existing exports and unused callbacks
+remain available without changing the selected graphics backend.
+
+## Hunk inventory and disposition
+
+Each subsection identifies a reference hunk or tightly coupled definition/use
+pair, its destination, and the equivalent present before this series. Paths in
+this section are target paths; remove `dlls/` to locate the flattened reference.
+
+### 1. ntdll/loader.c: native PE load notification (22434)
+
+After loading a non-builtin x86_64 PE image, pass its mapped address range to the
+Unix side. Destination: `dlls/ntdll/loader.c`. No previous equivalent. Keep the
+PE-side architecture guard; the Unix implementation gates all effects on the
+backend, Apple host, and supported OS.
+
+### 2. ntdll/unixlib.h: notification parameters and Unix call index
+
+Carry the start/end pointers and declare `unix_pe_module_loaded`. No previous
+equivalent. Append to Proton's existing Unix call enumeration, preserving all
+Proton-specific entries and their indices; do not replace the reference's whole
+enumeration. Both native and WoW64 tables must agree with that enumeration.
+
+### 3. ntdll/unix/loader.c: libd3dshared and Rosetta registration (22434)
+
+On Darwin 23/macOS 14 or newer, load the explicitly supplied dylib once, resolve
+`supports_non_native_code_regions` and `register_non_native_code_region`, and
+register native PE mappings when supported. Record the dylib's Mach-O `__TEXT`
+range for the ABI dispatchers below. No equivalent. The port requires both
+environment variables, uses explicit `RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL`, checks both
+optional functions before calling them, and validates the text segment.
+
+### 4. ntdll/unix/loader.c: native and WoW64 dispatch tables
+
+Append the notification handler to the native x86_64 table and a no-op/status
+stub to the matching 64-bit host's WoW64 table. No equivalent. A non-Apple
+x86_64 handler returns `STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`; no dylib loading is attempted.
+
+### 5. ntdll/loader.c and ntdll.spec: __wine_unix_call export (22435)
+
+Apple's PE DLLs import the public `__wine_unix_call` entry point. Already present
+as `compat___wine_unix_call` in Proton, with the same signature and forwarding
+behavior. No duplicate export or wrapper is added.
+
+### 6. ntdll Unix-library lookup and unixlib.h ABI
+
+Existing `load_unixlib_by_name` replaces the PE extension with `.so` and searches
+the architecture Unix directory; `NtQueryVirtualMemory`/the existing Unixlib
+machinery resolves its dispatch table. This already supports symlinks to a
+single dylib. The path variable in hunk 3 enables Rosetta/ABI support; it does
+not replace this search or automatically select Apple's PE DLLs. No changes
+needed to `include/wine/unixlib.h` or the normal library search. The older
+reference names `MemoryWineUnixFuncs`/`MemoryWineUnixWow64Funcs` and Proton
+names `MemoryWineLoadUnixLib`/`MemoryWineLoadUnixLibWow64` retain numeric values
+1000/1001 and the same module-to-function-table query contract.
+
+### 7. ntdll/unix/unix_private.h: mixed ABI dispatch (23015)
+
+The supplied dylib calls selected ntdll Unix exports with the Microsoft x64 ABI,
+while Wine's Unix callers use SysV. The reference checks the caller return
+address against the dylib text range, then jumps to the matching implementation.
+No equivalent. Keep Apple/x86_64 guards and preserve the registers used during
+the check; an unset range always takes the original SysV route.
+
+### 8. ntdll/unix/server.c: NtClose thunk (23015)
+
+Rename only the Unix implementation through `GPT_IMPORT` and add an `ms_abi`
+forwarder plus dispatcher. No equivalent. Keep Proton's actual close logic.
+
+### 9. ntdll/unix/sync.c: semaphore thunks (23015)
+
+Apply the same dispatch to `NtCreateSemaphore` and `NtReleaseSemaphore`. No
+equivalent. Preserve Proton synchronization implementations and fast paths.
+
+### 10. ntdll/unix/sync.c: event thunks (23015)
+
+Apply it to `NtCreateEvent`, `NtSetEvent`, `NtResetEvent`, `NtClearEvent`, and
+`NtPulseEvent`. No equivalent. Internal SysV calls still use the normal route.
+
+### 11. ntdll/unix/thread.c: NtCreateThreadEx thunk (23015)
+
+Forward all eleven arguments with the correct calling convention; do not
+replace Proton's thread setup implementation. No equivalent.
+
+### 12. winemac.drv/d3dmetal.c: exported function table (22435)
+
+Add the 24-pointer, 192-byte `macdrv_functions` data export Apple resolves from
+`winemac.so`. It provides display initialization, window data, Metal objects,
+main-thread dispatch, registry and USER operations. No equivalent. Preserve
+field order and x86_64 ABI assertions. This is a Unix data export, not a PE
+`.spec` export. Gate swapchain window-data creation on backend selection.
+
+### 13. winemac.drv/d3dmetal.c: legacy window data adapter
+
+Translate current `macdrv_win_data` into Apple's 120-byte legacy layout;
+create a current Wine client surface per swapchain and expose its Cocoa view.
+Store the locked current window data in a spare legacy slot until release.
+Existing client-surface and Metal object APIs provide the underlying mechanics,
+but this compatibility layout and hand-off are missing. Preserve creation
+before taking the window-data lock, and handle allocation failures. Unlike
+CrossOver, Proton no longer attaches surfaces in `client_surface_create`.
+Expose the existing `add_window_client_surface` helper through
+`include/wine/gdi_driver.h` (move its declaration out of
+`dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h`) and explicitly attach only bridge-created
+surfaces before taking the window-data lock. This preserves the normal
+Vulkan/OpenGL attachment paths and makes resize/detach work for D3DMetal.
+
+### 14. winemac.drv/d3dmetal.c: registry and USER wrappers
+
+Bridge ANSI registry calls back to PE advapi32 with `KeUserDispatchCallback`;
+wrap monitor/window APIs with win32u equivalents and expose `OnMainThread`.
+No equivalent table. These are the reference's ABI adapters, not additional
+registry-device enumeration logic. The PE callbacks use the Windows calling convention; the table wrappers use
+the Unix convention (`WINAPI` is empty under `WINE_UNIX_LIB`), as supplied.
+
+### 15. winemac.drv/unixlib.h: registry callback parameters
+
+Add three callback addresses to `init_params` and structures for create/open,
+query, and set-value calls. No equivalent. Unlike the reference, use `UINT64`
+for every result pointer: `UINT32 result` truncates x86_64 stack addresses.
+This is an internal PE/Unix contract, not Apple's external function-table ABI.
+
+### 16. winemac.drv/dllmain.c: PE registry callbacks
+
+Include winreg definitions, implement the three advapi32 callback handlers,
+and pass their addresses at initialization. No equivalent. No callbacks run
+until the D3DMetal table invokes them.
+
+### 17. winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c and macdrv.h: callback plumbing
+
+Declare/store the callback addresses, and propagate them through `wow64_init`
+so the shared initialization structure remains consistent. No equivalent.
+Also cache the host backend opt-in before Cocoa creates any Metal layers.
+
+### 18. winemac.drv/Makefile.in: bridge sources and imports
+
+Add `d3dmetal.c` (Unix pragma), `d3dmetal_objc.m` (Objective-C Unix source),
+and delayed advapi32 imports for the PE callbacks. Existing AppKit/Metal/
+QuartzCore link flags suffice. Do not import unrelated CrossOver icon sources.
+
+### 19. winemac.drv/macdrv.h and window.c: surface ownership
+
+Keep the swapchain client surfaces in a per-window CF array, releasing them
+when the window is destroyed. No equivalent ownership list; existing Wine
+client-surface detach logic is retained. Like the reference, this retains
+surfaces until window destruction, not until swapchain destruction.
+
+### 20. winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m: view association
+
+Add a client-surface pointer to `WineContentView` and getter/setter helpers so
+a Metal backing layer can identify its Wine surface. No equivalent. The
+pointer is only set by the D3DMetal bridge. Serialize changes on the Cocoa
+thread and clear it before detaching/disposing the view.
+
+### 21. winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m: backing-layer selection
+
+CrossOver unconditionally substitutes `WineMetalLayer` for `CAMetalLayer`.
+The port selects the subclass only for explicit D3DMetal on x86_64; default
+DXVK/MoltenVK and other architectures retain the original backing-layer class.
+
+### 22. winemac.drv/d3dmetal_objc.h and d3dmetal_objc.m
+
+Add `WineMetalLayer`, overriding `nextDrawable` to queue a presentation event
+for the associated client surface before obtaining the normal drawable. No
+equivalent. This lets win32u update/display the correct client surface for a
+swapchain that bypasses Wine's Vulkan/OpenGL presentation paths. The port
+inspects Cocoa views on the main thread, retains the event's surface, and
+releases it from `cocoa_event.m` even when events are discarded. This is a
+port-side lifetime fix; the reference queues an unowned pointer. Calling
+`nextDrawable` on the main thread executes the inspection directly.
+
+### 23. winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h: presentation event and declarations
+
+Add `CLIENT_SURFACE_PRESENTED`, its payload, and bridge helper declarations.
+No equivalent. Keep enum/debug-name ordering consistent and remain within the
+event-mask bit width; avoid importing CrossOver's separate Edit menu events.
+
+### 24. winemac.drv/event.c: presentation dispatch
+
+Add the debug name, include the event in `QS_POSTMESSAGE` processing, and call
+`client_surface_present` through the bridge handler. No equivalent. The handler
+must exist on every architecture on which the event switch is compiled.
+
+### 25. win32u/d3dkmt.c: LUID-based adapter opening
+
+`NtGdiDdDDIOpenAdapterFromLuid` already creates a handle even without a matching
+Vulkan physical device, as the reference does. Device creation and queries
+already work with that handle. No D3DMetal-specific LUID generator is present
+in the reference. Preserve this path and Proton's WDDM version reporting.
+
+### 26. win32u/d3dkmt.c: hardware scheduling (24905)
+
+CrossOver reports all three hardware-scheduling bits for explicit D3DMetal.
+Proton already has NVIDIA/Vulkan-specific WDDM 2.7 handling. Add a guarded Apple
+D3DMetal branch before the Vulkan-device requirement, validate the output size,
+and initialize all bits there. Leave the existing non-D3DMetal branch intact.
+
+### 27. win32u/sysparams.c and winemac.drv/display.c: device registry
+
+The existing display-device path creates GPU registry properties (including
+GPU LUID), monitor-to-GPU links, and Vulkan UUID/LUID mappings. The reference
+uses the same baseline machinery. No additional D3DMetal device registry
+population hunk was found; do not replace it wholesale.
+
+### 28. setupapi/devinst.c: GPU LUID helpers (23560)
+
+Diablo IV expects the SetupAPI GPU LUID to match Apple's DXGI adapter zero.
+Add the property key, executable-name check, and dynamic DXGI factory/adapter
+query. No equivalent. Replace CrossOver's version-resource heuristic (which
+can misidentify missing/other dxgi.dll files) with the exact backend variable;
+no new version.dll import is needed. Retain the single-GPU limitation.
+
+### 29. setupapi/devinst.c: SetupDiGetDevicePropertyW result override
+
+After a successful, correctly sized GPU-LUID property query for Diablo IV,
+substitute the DXGI LUID; retain the registry result on DXGI failure. No
+equivalent. Do not rewrite registry state or change other applications' LUIDs.
+This does not generalize identity matching to every SetupAPI/CM API.
+
+### 30. wined3d/adapter_gl.c: CS2 D3D9 driver identity (23042)
+
+CS2 queries its driver version through D3D9 even when rendering with D3D11.
+For Apple's OpenGL fallback incorrectly identified as NVIDIA 8800 GTX,
+CrossOver substitutes AMD RX 480 to match D3DMetal's vendor. No equivalent.
+Keep the executable/vendor/device tests and add explicit D3DMetal gating.
+Correct the reference's `GetModuleFileNameW` length to an element count.
+
+### 31. loader/wine.inf.in: fake DLLs (22435)
+
+CrossOver unconditionally installs `atidxx64.dll`, `nvapi64.dll`, and
+`nvngx.dll` placeholders in `FakeDllsWin64`. No equivalent for this group.
+Unconditional prefix changes conflict with the requested inert default. Put
+them in a separate, explicitly invoked `D3DMetal` install section instead;
+normal prefix initialization does not install them. See the test setup below.
+
+### 32. win32u/vulkan.c: backend-dependent Vulkan library (25909)
+
+The only matching environment hunk selects `CX_LIBVULKAN` when the backend is
+`wined3d`, not `d3dmetal`. It is not a D3DMetal dependency and is deliberately
+not ported. Existing MoltenVK lookup stays intact.
+
+### 33. Remaining supplied directories and unrelated hacks
+
+Searched all supplied `include`, `loader`, `ntdll`, `winemac.drv`, `win32u`,
+`setupapi`, `wined3d`, `winevulkan`, `d3d12`, `dxgi`, and `gdi32` sources for the
+named markers and transitive symbols. No further D3DMetal hunks were found in
+the latter graphics DLLs or public headers. CrossOver Edit-menu, application
+identity, icon, gamma, binary-patching, write-copy, and other unrelated hacks
+are excluded. Dependency numbers added to the original inventory are 23015,
+23042, and 24905; 25909 is a reviewed non-dependency.
+
+## Validation and Mac testing
+
+No Mac build or execution was possible in this workspace. These are local
+compile/structure checks, not evidence that D3DMetal renders successfully.
+
