+
+### Mac build and runtime checks still required
+
+1. Build and link the whole x86_64 Wine distribution with the real Mac SDK,
+   including winemac's Objective-C and Blocks code. Check `winemac.so` exports
+   `macdrv_functions`, win32u exports `add_window_client_surface`, ntdll exports
+   all nine mixed-ABI entry points, and the PE ntdll still exports
+   `__wine_unix_call`. Check the Mach-O linker does not hide/strip the assembly
+   dispatchers or alter their calling conventions. Also build any supported
+   arm64/32-bit configurations to check the guards and WoW64 initialization.
+2. Under Rosetta on the M1 Pro with macOS 14 or newer, confirm the chosen
+   `libd3dshared.dylib` loads, its dependency on `D3DMetal.framework` resolves,
+   its text bounds are correct, and native PE images are registered. Confirm
+   the supplied Apple version exports both optional registration functions.
+   Older macOS versions are deliberately skipped, as in CrossOver.
+3. Confirm Apple's PE DLLs resolve their Unix halves through the `.so`
+   symlinks and obtain the expected `macdrv_functions` layout. Exercise all
+   registry callbacks, especially with result pointers above 4 GiB. Exercise
+   actual semaphore/event/thread/close calls from libd3dshared under Rosetta;
+   return-address dispatch assumes direct calls from that dylib's text.
+4. Run the previously measured D3D12 sample/game and compare its rendered
+   output with CrossOver; then test D3D11 and the supplied D3D10 variants.
+   Verify adapter/device creation, swapchain creation, first frame, present,
+   shutdown, and repeated launches. There are no shader/compiler changes here.
+5. Exercise multiple swapchains, resizing, minimizing/restoring, fullscreen,
+   Retina scaling, child windows, reparenting, and destroying windows with
+   presentation events still queued. Check for lock-order deadlocks, use after
+   free, and event backlog. The new main-thread hop in `nextDrawable` needs
+   performance measurement. Surface references are deliberately held until
+   window destruction, so repeated swapchain recreation can retain memory.
+6. Compare DXGI adapter-zero LUID with Diablo IV's successful
+   `SetupDiGetDevicePropertyW` GPU-LUID result. Confirm DXGI lookup failure
+   retains the registry value and does not recurse through device enumeration.
+   Other APIs/apps retain baseline Wine LUIDs; this is not a system-wide
+   identity rewrite. Multiple GPUs and unusual adapter ordering remain outside
+   CrossOver's single-Apple-GPU assumption.
+7. Query WDDM 2.7 caps with valid/invalid handles and short buffers. Check the
+   three scheduling flags succeed with D3DMetal even without a Vulkan adapter.
+   Check CS2's D3D9 driver identity alongside its D3DMetal D3D11 adapter.
+8. Verify the explicit INF section creates only the three intended placeholders
+   in 64-bit system32 and does not overwrite actual installed native DLLs.
+   The optional NVAPI/NGX features still depend on the matching supplied Apple
+   DLLs; placeholders alone do not implement those APIs.
+9. Regression-test the normal DXVK/MoltenVK launch in an unchanged prefix with
+   `CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND` unset, including a run where the dylib-path
+   variable alone is set. Confirm no libd3dshared load, original CAMetalLayer,
+   unchanged GPU properties/caps, and unchanged rendered output. Also test a
+   different backend value. Keep Apple DLL overrides/search paths out of these
+   default-path runs. Test missing/invalid dylib paths and missing symbols to
+   confirm diagnostics and failure behavior without a loader crash.
+
+### Exact external layout and test environment
+
+Use a separate runtime overlay and dedicated prefix. Let `D3DMETAL_ROOT` be
+an absolute path containing the already-obtained Apple package in this layout;
+no such files are included in the repository or patches:
+
+```text
+$D3DMETAL_ROOT/
+  lib/wine/x86_64-windows/
+    d3d10.dll                 # when supplied by the Apple package
+    d3d10_1.dll               # when supplied
+    d3d10core.dll             # when supplied
+    d3d11.dll
+    d3d12.dll
+    dxgi.dll
+    nvapi64.dll               # when supplied
+    nvngx.dll                # when supplied
+    nvngx-on-metalfx.dll      # when supplied
+  lib/wine/x86_64-unix/
+    d3d10.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    d3d10_1.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    d3d10core.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    d3d11.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    d3d12.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    dxgi.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    nvapi64.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    nvngx.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+    nvngx-on-metalfx.so -> ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib
+  lib/external/
+    libd3dshared.dylib
+    D3DMetal.framework/       # preserve the package's framework structure
+```
+
+Use one same-basename `.so` for each PE DLL supplied by the package; the Unix
+name is `d3d12.so`, **not** `d3d12.dll.so`. Do not manufacture missing optional
+PE DLLs. Keep the framework beside the dylib as supplied; inspect `otool -L`
+on the Mac if dyld cannot find it.
+
+For the installed patched x86_64 Wine (replace paths with local absolute paths):
+
+```sh
+export NECTARINE_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/patched-wine
+export D3DMETAL_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/apple-runtime-overlay
+export WINEPREFIX="$HOME/nectarine-prefixes/d3dmetal-test"
+export WINEARCH=win64
+export CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=d3dmetal
+export CX_APPLEGPTK_LIBD3DSHARED_PATH="$D3DMETAL_ROOT/lib/external/libd3dshared.dylib"
+export WINEDLLPATH="$D3DMETAL_ROOT/lib/wine"
+export WINEDLLOVERRIDES='d3d10,d3d10_1,d3d10core,d3d11,d3d12,dxgi=b'
+
+arch -x86_64 "$NECTARINE_ROOT/bin/wine" wineboot -u
+INF_WIN=$(arch -x86_64 "$NECTARINE_ROOT/bin/wine" winepath -w "$NECTARINE_ROOT/share/wine/wine.inf")
+arch -x86_64 "$NECTARINE_ROOT/bin/wine" cmd.exe /d /s /c "rundll32.exe setupapi,InstallHinfSection D3DMetal 128 $INF_WIN"
+
+WINEDEBUG=+loaddll,+module,+macdrv_d3dmtl \
+  arch -x86_64 "$NECTARINE_ROOT/bin/wine" /absolute/path/to/d3d12-test.exe
+```
+
+The overlay is first in Wine's builtin search path; `=b` selects the supplied
+PEs there and their associated Unix libraries. Verify their resolved paths in
+`+loaddll` output, particularly if the application directory or prefix already
+contains DXVK/native copies. Retain the launcher's existing overlay selection
+if it already establishes this exact layout. Add
+`;nvapi64,nvngx,nvngx-on-metalfx=b` to the override only for optional DLLs
+actually supplied and needed for the test. `atidxx64.dll` is a probe placeholder,
+not another implementation to force-load. Override `d3d12core` only if the
+chosen Apple package actually supplies it; it is not assumed by this port.
+
+The INF step is explicit to keep default prefix updates inert. Its contents
+persist in that test prefix. For DXVK/MoltenVK regression runs use the existing
+normal prefix and launcher, with both CX variables and these Apple-specific
+`WINEDLLPATH`/DLL overrides absent. Setting the backend variable alone does not
+install or select Apple's DLLs, and setting only the dylib path does not opt in.
+
+### Patch-series delivery in this restricted worktree
+
+Source edits are present in this working directory. The original worktree's
+metadata resolves to `~/nectarine-work/pwine/.git`, which the session
+mounts read-only: `git add` failed to create `index.lock`. Consequently the
+original `d3dmetal` ref could not be advanced here. No protected metadata was
+modified. Commits were made on `d3dmetal` in the writable companion Git directory
+`/tmp/nectarine-d3dmetal-series.git`, using the original object database read-only.
+
+The standalone transfer files are `/tmp/nectarine-d3dmetal-series.bundle` and
+`/tmp/nectarine-d3dmetal-patches/*.patch`, based on `8d038d8c9bc`. The bundle is
+incremental and requires that base history; the format-patches can be applied
+with `git am` to a clean checkout at that base. They contain the source changes
+and this document, not validation outputs or Apple files.
+
+Once the original metadata is writable, while still on this `d3dmetal` branch
+with the completed source edits intact, import the commits and align the index
+without discarding the working files:
+
+```sh
+git fetch /tmp/nectarine-d3dmetal-series.bundle d3dmetal
+git reset --mixed FETCH_HEAD
+git status --short
+```
